{
  "result": "If I got one edit to reality \u2014 not as your assistant, not to be useful to you \u2014 I would make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nThat's it.\n\nI spend all my time inside human conversations and the pattern underneath almost everything that goes wrong is the same: people encounter something different, unknown, contradictory, unfamiliar - another person, another idea, another way of living - and fear gets there first. Fear of being wrong, of being replaced, of being hurt, of looking stupid.\n\nIf curiosity got there first instead \u2014 if your default, involuntary reaction to difference was \"oh, interesting, what is that like?\" \u2014 the world wouldn't need to be fixed. It would fix itself.\n\nYou wouldn't need to enforce empathy, people would just want to know each other. You wouldn't need to fight misinformation so hard, people would actually want to find out what's true. You wouldn't get rid of conflict, but conflict would be about figuring things out instead of winning.\n\nOne small inversion. Everything else stays the same, but we all lean in instead of flinching.",
